# gptokeyb mapping — the buttons become keys, so the LÖVE game only reads a keyboard.
# gptokeyb names buttons by POSITION, and these units report the face buttons
# mirrored: SDL "b" is the printed A, SDL "a" the printed B, SDL "y" the printed X
# and SDL "x" the printed Y. So the pairs are crossed on purpose:
#   b = x  printed A -> buy      a = z  printed B -> click
#   y = c  printed X -> advance/cast      x = v  printed Y -> nothing
back = tab
start = enter
a = z          # printed B -> click
b = x          # printed A -> buy
x = v          # printed Y -> unused
y = c          # printed X -> advance / cast
l1 = q
r1 = e
l2 = f          # zone select, back
r2 = g          # zone select, forward
up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right
left_analog_up = up
left_analog_down = down
left_analog_left = left
left_analog_right = right
